<decisions #add-domain-workbench-ui {
  version = "1"
}
(
  <decision #track.add_domain_workbench_ui.active_creation {
    priority = "P0"
    status = "accepted"
    durable_candidate = false
  }
  (
    <question ?>Should the G8 workbench UI track wait in pending or become active immediately?</?>
    <answer {
      selected = "active"
    }
    (
      <raw-answer ?>User requested autonomous mission progress; mission G8-T1 is ACTIVE.</?>
      <decision-text ?>Create `add-domain-workbench-ui` directly under `tracks/active` with `QuestionSeverity=auto`.</?>
      <rationale ?>G8 is already the next ready mission node, and no user preference question is blocking implementation.</?>
      <evidence ?>`mission.xml` G8-T1 ACTIVE; conversation instruction to continue the mission autonomously.</?>
    )
    >
  )
  >
  <decision #track.add_domain_workbench_ui.request_body_authority {
    priority = "P0"
    status = "accepted"
    durable_candidate = true
  }
  (
    <question ?>What is the source of truth for the execute request in the UI?</?>
    <answer {
      selected = "editor-json"
    }
    (
      <raw-answer ?>Mission HTTP contract states Preview JSON is the POST body.</?>
      <decision-text ?>The request JSON editor text is the submitted body authority; derived UI state must not reconstruct hidden request models.</?>
      <rationale ?>This prevents drift between preset preview, user edits, and server execution.</?>
      <evidence ?>`design/http-contract.md` exact request requirement and G7 exact-preset verification.</?>
    )
    >
  )
  >
  <decision #track.add_domain_workbench_ui.contract_owner {
    priority = "P0"
    status = "accepted"
    durable_candidate = false
  }
  (
    <question ?>Where should the frontend import Domain Operation DTO and parser authority from?</?>
    <answer {
      selected = "domain-operation-contracts"
    }
    (
      <raw-answer ?>Fresh planning review flagged that web-ide currently lacks the contract package dependency and web-shared must not become the domain DTO owner.</?>
      <decision-text ?>`packages/web-ide` should depend on `depa-data-domain-operation-contracts` for Domain Operation DTO/parser types while `depa-data-web-shared` remains a route and existing Kon shared package.</?>
      <rationale ?>This preserves the already frozen contract package ownership boundary and avoids a second frontend DTO model.</?>
      <evidence ?>`design/http-contract.md` capsule ownership and G8 planning AttractorCheck.</?>
    )
    >
  )
  >
)
>
